Copyright (C) 2026 YouGrow.AI Limited

This licence covers the files in the src/ee folder of the YouGrow repository. The rest of
the repository is under other licences: see section 6.


1. Definitions

"Licensor" means YouGrow.AI Limited.

"Software" means the files in the src/ee folder of the YouGrow repository, and any copy or
changed version of them, in whole or in part.

"Production use" means any use of the Software other than development and testing, for
example serving real users, holding real data or running a business with it.

"Subscription" means a paid agreement with the Licensor that allows Production use for a
set term.

"Licence key" means a key issued by the Licensor that names the licensee, the Enterprise
features it covers, the number of Users it allows and the date it ends.

"User" means a person who can sign in to a deployment that includes the Software.

"You" means the person or organisation using the Software under this licence.


2. Development and testing

You may read, copy and change the Software, and run it for development and testing, at no
charge. You may share copies of the Software, changed or not, as long as they stay under
this licence. Keep this licence and the copyright notice with every copy.


3. Production use

Production use needs an active Subscription and a Licence key that covers at least the
number of Users of the deployment. Without both, you may not put the Software into
Production use.


4. The licence key check

You may not remove, disable or work around the Licence key check, or any limit a Licence
key sets, and you may not help anyone else to do so.


5. Changes

Any change you make to the Software stays under this licence, and so does any copy of a
changed version.


6. Code outside src/ee

This licence does not cover code outside the src/ee folder. LICENSING.md, at the root of
the repository, says which licence covers each part.


7. No warranty, and a limit on liability

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,
INCLUDING THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
NONINFRINGEMENT. AS FAR AS THE LAW ALLOWS, THE LICENSOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, LOSS
OR DAMAGE, DIRECT OR INDIRECT, THAT ARISES FROM THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE.


8. Ending

This licence ends automatically if you break any of its terms. When it ends, your rights
under it end too, and you must stop any Production use of the Software.


